# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both image builds use the repository root as their context, so without this
# every `docker build` uploads the Flutter build output, two `node_modules`
# trees and a local virtualenv before running a single instruction.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that actually breaks something rather than merely
# being slow: `COPY apps/portal/ ./` would drop a host-built tree on top of the
# `npm ci` the stage just ran, so the image would build against whatever
# happened to be installed on the machine that built it -- including native
# binaries compiled for a different platform.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

node_modules/
apps/website/dist/
apps/portal/dist/

apps/mobile/build/
apps/mobile/.dart_tool/
apps/connector/build/
apps/connector/dist/

# Large, built on Windows, and bind-mounted at runtime rather than baked in.
deploy/uat/downloads/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log
